WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:03.225 line:85%
Here is our augmented-reality mobile app,

2
00:00:03.225 --> 00:00:07.180 line:85%
designed to understand how an ionization
machine works.

3
00:00:07.630 --> 00:00:09.756 line:85%
Let's start with the first feature.

4
00:00:09.756 --> 00:00:14.060 line:85%
We point the camera at the marker and the
model appears in augmented reality.

5
00:00:14.510 --> 00:00:17.812 line:85%
Now let's tap Play to start the animation.

6
00:00:17.812 --> 00:00:22.610 line:85%
We can follow the machine's normal
operation, step by step.

7
00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:27.370 line:85%
During loading, the transfer arm places the
wafer on the platen.

8
00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:28.978 line:85%
At each step,

9
00:00:28.978 --> 00:00:35.720 line:85%
a description appears on screen to explain
the sequence of operations and the role of
the machine's components.

10
00:00:36.170 --> 00:00:39.909 line:85%
The animation continues to the end of the
operating cycle.

11
00:00:39.909 --> 00:00:43.477 line:85%
During unloading, the transfer arm removes
the wafer,

12
00:00:43.477 --> 00:00:44.950 line:85%
then the lid opens.

13
00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:48.781 line:85%
Once the cycle is complete, we can browse
the steps,

14
00:00:48.781 --> 00:00:51.940 line:85%
pause the animation or restart it at any
time.

15
00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:54.783 line:85%
On to the second feature:

16
00:00:54.783 --> 00:00:58.420 line:85%
real-time monitoring through augmented
reality.

17
00:00:58.870 --> 00:01:00.085 line:85%
For this demonstration,

18
00:01:00.085 --> 00:01:03.680 line:85%
we use an emulator that reproduces the
machine's operation.

19
00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:06.191 line:85%
The data is sent over MQTT,

20
00:01:06.191 --> 00:01:09.940 line:85%
which updates the digital twin's state in
our app.

21
00:01:10.390 --> 00:01:15.188 line:85%
As you can see, we start by watching the
machine's normal operation,

22
00:01:15.188 --> 00:01:16.400 line:85%
with no failure.

23
00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:21.684 line:85%
Next, we simulate three cooling-circuit
failures.

24
00:01:21.684 --> 00:01:23.980 line:85%
The first is a pressure drop.

25
00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:29.220 line:85%
We select it on the control box and run the
scenario at higher speed.

26
00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:34.303 line:85%
Thanks to the artificial intelligence
models, the system monitors the
measurements,

27
00:01:34.303 --> 00:01:37.440 line:85%
detects anomalies and predicts the risk of
failure.

28
00:01:37.890 --> 00:01:42.526 line:85%
The app also shows the estimated time before
the machine fails,

29
00:01:42.526 --> 00:01:45.670 line:85%
which makes it possible to plan maintenance
in advance.

30
00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:49.610 line:85%
We move to the second type of failure, high
pressure.

31
00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:52.405 line:85%
As you can see on the model,

32
00:01:52.405 --> 00:01:57.250 line:85%
the pressure gauge needle moves to the
right, showing a pressure increase.

33
00:01:57.700 --> 00:02:02.340 line:85%
Finally, we move to the third scenario, a
leak in the circuit.

34
00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:09.554 line:85%
As with the previous anomalies, the system
continuously analyzes the data and estimates
the remaining useful life,

35
00:02:09.554 --> 00:02:12.040 line:85%
shown directly on the digital twin.
